{"create_document":{"desc":"Create a new document and return {document_id, branch_id}. The document starts with a single empty paragraph, so follow up with insert_block calls (position end) in the same turn to fill it. Omit parent_id to create it at the organisation root.","has_params_one_of":true,"json_schema":{"properties":{"icon":{"description":"Iconify identifier, as \"collection:name\". The product's own icons are MingCute fills (e.g. \"mingcute:file-code-fill\"); prefer one so the document matches the rest of the sidebar. Defaults to \"mingcute:document-2-fill\" when empty.","type":"string"},"name":{"description":"Display name for the new document.","type":"string"},"parent_id":{"description":"Optional parent document id. Omit to create at the org root.","type":"string"}},"required":["name"],"type":"object"},"name":"create_document"},"delete_block":{"desc":"Delete one block by uid, including anything nested inside it. Its comments, hooks and files go with it and cannot be restored, so use move_block when the aim is to reorder and update_block_text when the aim is new wording. Returns {deleted: uid}.","has_params_one_of":true,"json_schema":{"properties":{"block_uid":{"description":"The uid of the block to delete.","type":"string"},"document_id":{"description":"The target document id.","type":"string"}},"required":["document_id","block_uid"],"type":"object"},"name":"delete_block"},"delete_document":{"desc":"Delete a document and every document nested under it. The whole subtree goes and cannot be restored, so check the tree with list_documents first, and use update_document when the aim is to relocate rather than remove. Returns {document_id, deleted}.","has_params_one_of":true,"json_schema":{"properties":{"document_id":{"description":"The document id to delete.","type":"string"}},"required":["document_id"],"type":"object"},"name":"delete_document"},"get_document":{"desc":"Read one document: its name, icon, parent_id, protected flag and updated_at, followed by one row per block with the block's uid, kind, flattened text, depth, parent_uid and the few attrs that matter for reading (heading level, callout icon, code language, task checked). Use it as the way to read a document before editing it; protected true means every write is refused. Rows marked has_children hold nested blocks the rows do not list, and read_block returns those when you need them.","has_params_one_of":true,"json_schema":{"properties":{"document_id":{"description":"The document id.","type":"string"}},"required":["document_id"],"type":"object"},"name":"get_document"},"get_prometheus_metadata":{"desc":"List the metrics a Prometheus data source exposes, with each metric's type, help text and unit. Use it to find the metric names to write a PromQL query against instead of guessing them.","has_params_one_of":true,"json_schema":{"properties":{"data_source_id":{"description":"The data source id, from list_data_sources.","type":"string"}},"required":["data_source_id"],"type":"object"},"name":"get_prometheus_metadata"},"get_sql_metadata":{"desc":"List the tables and their columns in a PostgreSQL, MariaDB or MySQL data source, plus the default schema. Read it before writing a query so the table and column names are the real ones.","has_params_one_of":true,"json_schema":{"properties":{"data_source_id":{"description":"The data source id, from list_data_sources.","type":"string"}},"required":["data_source_id"],"type":"object"},"name":"get_sql_metadata"},"get_sql_query_labels":{"desc":"Run a SQL query limited to one row and return its string columns with an example value each, which are the columns a chart would treat as series labels. Use it to check what a query returns before charting it; it is cheaper than query_sql.","has_params_one_of":true,"json_schema":{"properties":{"data_source_id":{"description":"The data source id, from list_data_sources.","type":"string"},"from":{"description":"Optional. Range start as an RFC3339 timestamp. Defaults to an hour before 'to'.","type":"string"},"query":{"description":"The SQL query to probe. $__ macros are expanded as they are for a metric block.","type":"string"},"to":{"description":"Optional. Range end as an RFC3339 timestamp. Defaults to now.","type":"string"}},"required":["data_source_id","query"],"type":"object"},"name":"get_sql_query_labels"},"insert_block":{"desc":"Insert one canonical block into a document. position start or end puts it at the document's start or end; before or after puts it beside the block reference_block_uid names, which stays in place. The block has to be legal where it lands: the document root takes every type except titled_code, metric and split_doc_param_list, and a reference inside a split_doc or metric_grid takes only what that container holds. Returns the summary rows of the new block and everything nested in it, uids included, with depth counted from the block itself.","has_params_one_of":true,"json_schema":{"properties":{"block":{"description":"A canonical block. Which fields apply depends on type; supply only that type's own.","properties":{"attrs":{"description":"Per-type attributes. Required where the type says so: heading level, titled_code title, image and figma src. Also code language, callout icon, image alt and width, and a metric's chart configuration, whose width is compact, standard or wide.","properties":{"level":{"description":"heading: the level. Required on a heading.","enum":[1,2,3],"type":"integer"},"refreshInterval":{"description":"metric: how often the chart re-queries.","enum":["5s","10s","30s","1m","5m","15m","30m","1h","2h","1d"],"type":"string"},"simulationPreset":{"description":"metric: draws this generated series in place of the query's own result, for a block documenting a metric that has no real data yet. Omit it to chart the query.","enum":["cpu_usage","memory_usage","disk_usage","http_requests","http_latency","error_rate"],"type":"string"},"timeRange":{"description":"metric: the window queried.","enum":["last_5_minutes","last_15_minutes","last_30_minutes","last_1_hour","last_3_hours","last_6_hours","last_12_hours","last_24_hours","last_2_days","last_7_days","last_30_days","last_90_days","last_6_months","last_1_year","last_2_years","last_5_years","today","yesterday","today_so_far","this_week","this_week_so_far","this_month","this_month_so_far","this_year","this_year_so_far","previous_week","previous_month","previous_year"],"type":"string"},"unitType":{"description":"metric: the unit values are read in. With custom, put the label in unitCustom.","enum":["custom","nanoseconds","microseconds","milliseconds","seconds","minutes","hours","days","bytes","kilobytes","megabytes","gigabytes","terabytes","bits","kilobits","megabits","gigabits","terabits","percent0to100","percent0to1"],"type":"string"},"visualizationType":{"description":"metric: the chart kind.","enum":["line_chart","bar_chart","gauge_chart"],"type":"string"}},"type":"object"},"children":{"description":"Blocks nested under a single list entry. A list entry is a paragraph; anything else nested under it goes here, never in the entry itself and never in a second entry.","type":"array"},"header":{"description":"split_doc_param_list heading, as plain text.","type":"string"},"items":{"description":"Entries of bullet_list and ordered_list, which are paragraphs; items of metric_grid, and of blockquote or callout when not using text.","type":"array"},"left":{"description":"split_doc concept side. Must start with a level-1 heading; split_doc_param_list is legal only here.","type":"array"},"params":{"description":"split_doc_param_list rows, each {name, type, description}.","type":"array"},"right":{"description":"split_doc example side. Holds titled_code or metric only, and is the one place titled_code is legal.","type":"array"},"task_items":{"description":"Rows of task_list, each {checked, block}.","type":"array"},"text":{"description":"Inline text for paragraph, heading, blockquote, code, titled_code, mermaid and callout. Raw inside code, titled_code and mermaid; minimal markdown elsewhere. One block is one paragraph; a newline inside text does not start a new one.","type":"string"},"type":{"description":"The block's canonical type.","enum":["paragraph","heading","blockquote","bullet_list","ordered_list","task_list","callout","code","titled_code","mermaid","horizontal_rule","image","figma","metric","metric_grid","split_doc","split_doc_param_list"],"type":"string"},"uid":{"description":"Leave unset. Uids are generated server-side and are the handle later edits use.","type":"string"}},"required":["type"],"type":"object"},"document_id":{"description":"The target document id.","type":"string"},"position":{"description":"Where the block lands: before or after the reference block, or at the start or end of the document.","enum":["before","after","start","end"],"type":"string"},"reference_block_uid":{"description":"The uid of the block to insert beside. Required with before and after; leave it out with start and end.","type":"string"}},"required":["document_id","position","block"],"type":"object"},"name":"insert_block"},"list_data_sources":{"desc":"List the organisation's data sources. Returns id, name, type (prometheus, postgresql, mariadb, mysql) and connection status. Start here: every other data-source tool takes an id from this list, and the type decides which of them serves it.","has_params_one_of":true,"json_schema":{"properties":{},"type":"object"},"name":"list_data_sources"},"list_documents":{"desc":"List the organisation's documents as a tree of {id, name, children}. Use it to find a document by name or to see what sits under a parent; use search_documents when you are looking for content rather than a title. Pass parent_id to get only that document's direct children, or omit it for the whole organisation.","has_params_one_of":true,"json_schema":{"properties":{"parent_id":{"description":"Optional. Return only the direct children of this document. Omit for the full tree.","type":"string"}},"type":"object"},"name":"list_documents"},"list_prometheus_label_names":{"desc":"List the label names present in a Prometheus data source, optionally only those on the series the matchers select. Pair it with list_prometheus_label_values to build a filtered PromQL query.","has_params_one_of":true,"json_schema":{"properties":{"data_source_id":{"description":"The data source id, from list_data_sources.","type":"string"},"from":{"description":"Optional. Range start as an RFC3339 timestamp. Defaults to an hour before 'to'.","type":"string"},"matchers":{"description":"Optional. PromQL series selectors, e.g. [\"up\", \"{job=\\\"api\\\"}\"].","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"to":{"description":"Optional. Range end as an RFC3339 timestamp. Defaults to now.","type":"string"}},"required":["data_source_id"],"type":"object"},"name":"list_prometheus_label_names"},"list_prometheus_label_values":{"desc":"List the values a label takes in a Prometheus data source, optionally only on the series the matchers select. Use it to discover the concrete label values a query should filter on.","has_params_one_of":true,"json_schema":{"properties":{"data_source_id":{"description":"The data source id, from list_data_sources.","type":"string"},"from":{"description":"Optional. Range start as an RFC3339 timestamp. Defaults to an hour before 'to'.","type":"string"},"label":{"description":"The label whose values to list, e.g. \"job\".","type":"string"},"matchers":{"description":"Optional. PromQL series selectors, e.g. [\"up\", \"{job=\\\"api\\\"}\"].","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"to":{"description":"Optional. Range end as an RFC3339 timestamp. Defaults to now.","type":"string"}},"required":["data_source_id","label"],"type":"object"},"name":"list_prometheus_label_values"},"list_prometheus_series":{"desc":"List the series matching a set of selectors in a Prometheus data source, each as its full label set. Use it to see which label combinations a metric actually has before querying it.","has_params_one_of":true,"json_schema":{"properties":{"data_source_id":{"description":"The data source id, from list_data_sources.","type":"string"},"from":{"description":"Optional. Range start as an RFC3339 timestamp. Defaults to an hour before 'to'.","type":"string"},"matchers":{"description":"PromQL series selectors, e.g. [\"up\", \"{job=\\\"api\\\"}\"].","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"to":{"description":"Optional. Range end as an RFC3339 timestamp. Defaults to now.","type":"string"}},"required":["data_source_id","matchers"],"type":"object"},"name":"list_prometheus_series"},"move_block":{"desc":"Move an existing block before or after another block in the same document. The block keeps its uid, attrs and nested content, so comments, hooks and files attached to it stay attached; deleting it and inserting a copy would lose them. The landing spot has to accept the block's type, by the same rule insert_block applies. Returns the summary rows of the moved block and everything nested in it.","has_params_one_of":true,"json_schema":{"properties":{"block_uid":{"description":"The uid of the block to move.","type":"string"},"document_id":{"description":"The target document id.","type":"string"},"position":{"description":"Landing side relative to the reference block.","enum":["before","after"],"type":"string"},"reference_block_uid":{"description":"The uid of the block to move relative to.","type":"string"}},"required":["document_id","block_uid","position","reference_block_uid"],"type":"object"},"name":"move_block"},"query_prometheus":{"desc":"Run a PromQL range query against a Prometheus data source over the given window. Returns the raw result by default; with chart_type set it instead describes what a metric block would render, which is how to check a query before writing it into a block.","has_params_one_of":true,"json_schema":{"properties":{"chart_type":{"description":"Optional. One of line_chart, bar_chart, gauge_chart. When set, the result describes what the metric block would draw (render status, series count, and each series' labels, point count and endpoints) instead of the raw data. Use it to check a query before putting it in a metric block; omit it when you need the values themselves.","type":"string"},"data_source_id":{"description":"The data source id, from list_data_sources.","type":"string"},"from":{"description":"Optional. Range start as an RFC3339 timestamp. Defaults to an hour before 'to'.","type":"string"},"query":{"description":"The PromQL expression to run.","type":"string"},"to":{"description":"Optional. Range end as an RFC3339 timestamp. Defaults to now.","type":"string"}},"required":["data_source_id","query"],"type":"object"},"name":"query_prometheus"},"query_sql":{"desc":"Run a read-only query against a PostgreSQL, MariaDB or MySQL data source. Returns columns and rows by default; with chart_type set it instead describes what a metric block would render, which is how to check a query before writing it into a block. $__ macros ($__timeFilter, $__timeGroupAlias and the rest) are expanded against the window.","has_params_one_of":true,"json_schema":{"properties":{"chart_type":{"description":"Optional. One of line_chart, bar_chart, gauge_chart. When set, the result describes what the metric block would draw (render status, series count, and each series' labels, point count and endpoints) instead of the raw data. Use it to check a query before putting it in a metric block; omit it when you need the values themselves.","type":"string"},"data_source_id":{"description":"The data source id, from list_data_sources.","type":"string"},"from":{"description":"Optional. Range start as an RFC3339 timestamp. Defaults to an hour before 'to'.","type":"string"},"query":{"description":"The SQL query to run. For a chart, select a time column aliased \"time\" plus one or more numeric columns.","type":"string"},"to":{"description":"Optional. Range end as an RFC3339 timestamp. Defaults to now.","type":"string"}},"required":["data_source_id","query"],"type":"object"},"name":"query_sql"},"read_block":{"desc":"Return the full canonical content of one block by uid, including any nested children. Use it only when get_document's rows are not enough: to edit a split_doc, a nested list or a split_doc_param_list, whose inner structure has to be written back in full. Fails when the uid is not in the document.","has_params_one_of":true,"json_schema":{"properties":{"block_uid":{"description":"The block uid to fetch.","type":"string"},"document_id":{"description":"The document id.","type":"string"}},"required":["document_id","block_uid"],"type":"object"},"name":"read_block"},"read_tool_output":{"desc":"Retrieve the full output of an earlier tool call that was too large to keep in the conversation. Pass the path shown in the truncation notice.","has_params_one_of":true,"json_schema":{"properties":{"file_path":{"description":"The stored output path from the truncation notice.","type":"string"}},"required":["file_path"],"type":"object"},"name":"read_tool_output"},"replace_block":{"desc":"Replace a block by uid with a new block in the same position. The old block's uid, content and children are all gone unless the new block carries them, so use it to change a block's type or its whole structure. For a wording change use update_block_text, and for an attribute change update_block_attrs; both keep the uid, which comments, hooks and files hang off. Returns the summary rows of the new block and everything nested in it, uids included, with depth counted from the block itself.","has_params_one_of":true,"json_schema":{"properties":{"block":{"description":"A canonical block. Which fields apply depends on type; supply only that type's own.","properties":{"attrs":{"description":"Per-type attributes. Required where the type says so: heading level, titled_code title, image and figma src. Also code language, callout icon, image alt and width, and a metric's chart configuration, whose width is compact, standard or wide.","properties":{"level":{"description":"heading: the level. Required on a heading.","enum":[1,2,3],"type":"integer"},"refreshInterval":{"description":"metric: how often the chart re-queries.","enum":["5s","10s","30s","1m","5m","15m","30m","1h","2h","1d"],"type":"string"},"simulationPreset":{"description":"metric: draws this generated series in place of the query's own result, for a block documenting a metric that has no real data yet. Omit it to chart the query.","enum":["cpu_usage","memory_usage","disk_usage","http_requests","http_latency","error_rate"],"type":"string"},"timeRange":{"description":"metric: the window queried.","enum":["last_5_minutes","last_15_minutes","last_30_minutes","last_1_hour","last_3_hours","last_6_hours","last_12_hours","last_24_hours","last_2_days","last_7_days","last_30_days","last_90_days","last_6_months","last_1_year","last_2_years","last_5_years","today","yesterday","today_so_far","this_week","this_week_so_far","this_month","this_month_so_far","this_year","this_year_so_far","previous_week","previous_month","previous_year"],"type":"string"},"unitType":{"description":"metric: the unit values are read in. With custom, put the label in unitCustom.","enum":["custom","nanoseconds","microseconds","milliseconds","seconds","minutes","hours","days","bytes","kilobytes","megabytes","gigabytes","terabytes","bits","kilobits","megabits","gigabits","terabits","percent0to100","percent0to1"],"type":"string"},"visualizationType":{"description":"metric: the chart kind.","enum":["line_chart","bar_chart","gauge_chart"],"type":"string"}},"type":"object"},"children":{"description":"Blocks nested under a single list entry. A list entry is a paragraph; anything else nested under it goes here, never in the entry itself and never in a second entry.","type":"array"},"header":{"description":"split_doc_param_list heading, as plain text.","type":"string"},"items":{"description":"Entries of bullet_list and ordered_list, which are paragraphs; items of metric_grid, and of blockquote or callout when not using text.","type":"array"},"left":{"description":"split_doc concept side. Must start with a level-1 heading; split_doc_param_list is legal only here.","type":"array"},"params":{"description":"split_doc_param_list rows, each {name, type, description}.","type":"array"},"right":{"description":"split_doc example side. Holds titled_code or metric only, and is the one place titled_code is legal.","type":"array"},"task_items":{"description":"Rows of task_list, each {checked, block}.","type":"array"},"text":{"description":"Inline text for paragraph, heading, blockquote, code, titled_code, mermaid and callout. Raw inside code, titled_code and mermaid; minimal markdown elsewhere. One block is one paragraph; a newline inside text does not start a new one.","type":"string"},"type":{"description":"The block's canonical type.","enum":["paragraph","heading","blockquote","bullet_list","ordered_list","task_list","callout","code","titled_code","mermaid","horizontal_rule","image","figma","metric","metric_grid","split_doc","split_doc_param_list"],"type":"string"},"uid":{"description":"Leave unset. Uids are generated server-side and are the handle later edits use.","type":"string"}},"required":["type"],"type":"object"},"block_uid":{"description":"The uid of the block being replaced.","type":"string"},"document_id":{"description":"The target document id.","type":"string"}},"required":["document_id","block_uid","block"],"type":"object"},"name":"replace_block"},"search_documents":{"desc":"Full-text search across every document in the organisation for blocks whose text matches the query. Returns hits with document_id, document_name, block_uid and text. Use it to find where a topic is discussed or which documents the user might mean; use list_documents when you know the title. A hit names the innermost block holding the text, which may sit below anything get_document lists; read_block resolves it.","has_params_one_of":true,"json_schema":{"properties":{"limit":{"description":"Maximum number of hits to return. Defaults to 20; cap is 50.","type":"integer"},"query":{"description":"The full-text search query (typo-tolerant, matches block text).","type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"type":"object"},"name":"search_documents"},"update_block_attrs":{"desc":"Set or override named attributes on an existing block, such as a heading's level or a callout's icon. Attributes not mentioned are kept and uid cannot change. Values are validated for the block's type, so a level outside 1 to 3 or a metric width other than compact, standard or wide is rejected. Use replace_block when the type itself has to change. Returns the summary rows of the block and everything nested in it, attrs as they now stand.","has_params_one_of":true,"json_schema":{"properties":{"attrs":{"description":"Attribute keys and values to set (e.g. {\"level\": 2}, {\"icon\": \"lucide:warning\"}).","type":"object"},"block_uid":{"description":"The uid of the block whose attrs should be updated.","type":"string"},"document_id":{"description":"The target document id.","type":"string"}},"required":["document_id","block_uid","attrs"],"type":"object"},"name":"update_block_attrs"},"update_block_text":{"desc":"Replace the inline text of one text-bearing block: paragraph, heading, blockquote, code, titled_code, mermaid, or a callout written with text. Type, attrs and uid are kept, so this is the tool for wording changes. Text follows the canonical markdown subset (**bold**, *italic*, _underline_, ~~strike~~, backtick code, [label](url)), and is raw in code, titled_code and mermaid. One block is one paragraph; to add a paragraph, insert a block instead. Returns the block's summary row with the new text.","has_params_one_of":true,"json_schema":{"properties":{"block_uid":{"description":"The uid of the block whose text should be replaced.","type":"string"},"document_id":{"description":"The target document id.","type":"string"},"text":{"description":"New inline text in canonical markdown.","type":"string"}},"required":["document_id","block_uid","text"],"type":"object"},"name":"update_block_text"},"update_document":{"desc":"Change a document's name, icon or place in the tree, any combination in one call; content is untouched. Give only the fields to change: name is the new display name, icon an Iconify identifier as \"collection:name\" (the product's own icons are MingCute fills, e.g. \"mingcute:rocket-fill\", so prefer one to match the sidebar), and parent_id the new parent, or an empty string for the organisation root. A call with none of the three is refused, and a parent that is the document itself or one of its descendants fails. Returns {document_id} with the fields that changed.","has_params_one_of":true,"json_schema":{"properties":{"document_id":{"description":"The document id.","type":"string"},"icon":{"description":"Optional. The new icon identifier; omit to keep the current one.","type":"string"},"name":{"description":"Optional. The new display name; omit to keep the current one.","type":"string"},"parent_id":{"description":"Optional. The new parent document id, or an empty string to move the document to the organisation root; omit to leave it where it is.","type":"string"}},"required":["document_id"],"type":"object"},"name":"update_document"}}